 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 05:15:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 027/154] fix: ROOT CAUSE - top chrome must not get a page
 context menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The diagnostic named it on the first reproduction:

    Atrium: no AutocompleteClassifier for profile
      path=System Profile otr=1 guest=0 system=1 regular=0

Atrium's chrome layer - sidebar, pill, foyer - is WebUI hosted on the SYSTEM
profile: AtriumChromeContext builds its context from
ProfileManager::GetSystemProfilePath(). Right-clicking selected text in the
sidebar therefore built a full PAGE context menu against a system profile, and
that menu assumes a content profile throughout. AppendSearchProvider alone
dereferences AutocompleteClassifierFactory and TemplateURLServiceFactory,
neither of which serves a system profile (no .WithSystem(), which defaults to
kNone), so the browser process segfaulted and took the session with it.

Guarding those two services was the mitigation shipped first, and it is
whack-a-mole: every profile-keyed service this menu grows in future is the same
crash again. The rule is that a page menu has no business on chrome content.
These surfaces build their own DOM menus - see sidebar-menu.js - and
the native one was never wanted. No page content is hosted on the system
profile in this browser, so keying on it is both safe and accurate.

The two service guards stay. They cost nothing, they are correct on their own
terms, and their logging is what turned four rounds of theorising into one
named profile.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../render_view_context_menu.cc               | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
index c65527f7da9b0..4d34131165ff1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
@@ -1246,6 +1246,27 @@ bool RenderViewContextMenu::IsInProgressiveWebApp() const {
 }
 
 void RenderViewContextMenu::InitMenu() {
+  // ATRIUM: top chrome gets no PAGE context menu.
+  //
+  // Atrium's chrome layer - the sidebar, the pill, the foyer - is WebUI hosted
+  // on the SYSTEM profile (AtriumChromeContext uses
+  // ProfileManager::GetSystemProfilePath). Right-clicking selected text there
+  // built this menu, and it assumes a content profile throughout: the search
+  // section alone dereferences AutocompleteClassifierFactory and
+  // TemplateURLServiceFactory, neither of which serves a system profile, so
+  // the BROWSER process segfaulted and took the session with it.
+  //
+  // Guarding those two services individually is whack-a-mole - every future
+  // profile-keyed service this menu grows is the same crash. The rule is that
+  // a page menu has no business on chrome content at all: these surfaces build
+  // their own DOM menus (see sidebar-menu.js) and the native one was never
+  // wanted. The system profile hosts no page content in this browser, so
+  // keying on it is safe as well as accurate.
+  if (Profile* const profile = GetProfile();
+      profile && profile->IsSystemProfile()) {
+    return;
+  }
+
   RenderViewContextMenuBase::InitMenu();
 
   const bool use_simplified_menu_for_text_selection =
